<LegalDocument
  title="Privacy Policy"
  updated="October 31, 2026"
  description="How Impact Recap handles contact-form messages, hosting logs, YouTube embeds, Google reCAPTCHA, and the other third-party services used to publish this site."
>
  <p>
    This notice describes how Impact Recap ("we") handles information when you use <a href="https://impact-recap.com/">https://impact-recap.com</a>. It is a general
    description of this website. It is not legal advice, and it does not promise a
    particular legal outcome.
  </p>

  <h2>What this notice covers</h2>
  <p>
    It covers this website: the sermon recap pages, the library, and the contact form.
    There is no account, no app, and no payment checkout. Sermon pages are published
    for anyone to read.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you give us</h2>
  <p>If you use the contact form, we receive the details you submit:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Name</li>
    <li>Email address</li>
    <li>Subject</li>
    <li>Message</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Please do not send government ID numbers, financial account numbers, or other
    sensitive information through the form. We use what you send to reply, to fix
    problems you report, and to operate the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Information collected while you browse</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Netlify. Like most hosts, Netlify may record technical
    details that a browser sends with a request, such as IP address, browser type,
    and the page requested, in order to deliver and protect the site. We do not run
    our own analytics product, and we do not sell personal information.
  </p>
  <p>Pages also load a few outside services:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Sermon images are requested from YouTube's image host (i.ytimg.com).</li>
    <li>A sermon page embeds the YouTube player.</li>
    <li>Typefaces are loaded from Google Fonts.</li>
    <li>Layout and icon stylesheets are loaded from a Bootstrap CDN and from cdnjs.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Those providers receive the technical data a browser sends with the request,
    including an IP address. If you press play on an embedded video, YouTube's own
    privacy policy applies to that player.
  </p>

  <h2>Google reCAPTCHA</h2>
  <p>
    Contact forms on this site use Google reCAPTCHA. See Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to questions, corrections, and bug reports.</li>
    <li>To operate, secure, and debug the site.</li>
    <li>To reduce spam on the contact form.</li>
    <li>To meet a legal duty if one applies.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not use contact details for a mailing list. We do not ask you to create
    an account or to sign in with a social network.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else may process it</h2>
  <p>We share information only as needed to run the site:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Netlify, which hosts the site, stores form submissions, and may filter spam.</li>
    <li>Google, for reCAPTCHA, fonts, and YouTube embeds and thumbnails.</li>
    <li>The CDN operators that serve the Bootstrap and icon stylesheets.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A form message may also be emailed to the person who operates the site so they
    can read it. These providers may process information in the United States or in
    other countries where they operate. We do not control their systems.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Impact Recap does not set its own advertising cookies. The services listed above
    may set or read cookies when their content loads, especially YouTube and
    reCAPTCHA. You can control cookies in your browser. Blocking them may stop the
    video player or the form check from working.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not change the site in response to a Do Not Track signal. Outside services
    may still collect technical data as described above.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Contact messages are kept long enough to respond and to handle follow-up. They
    may remain in Netlify's form storage until they are deleted. This notice does
    not set a fixed number of months or years. Server logs are kept on the host's
    schedule, which we do not control.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We rely on the host and on ordinary care when reading messages. No website can
    promise that a transmission or a stored message will stay perfectly secure.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The site is a general-audience collection of sermon recaps. It is not directed
    to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from
    them. If you believe a child under 13 sent personal information through the
    form, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your requests</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have a right to ask for access, correction,
    or deletion of personal information you sent us. Use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> and say what you are asking for. We will
    consider the request as applicable law requires. We may need enough detail to
    find the message.
  </p>

  <h2>Other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Links to YouTube, and the Instagram, YouTube, and Facebook links in the header,
    go to Impact Church's own channels or to YouTube. Their policies apply once you
    leave this site. We do not control those sites.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this notice changes, we will post the new version on this page and update the
    date above. The posted version is the current one.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this notice go through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
    We do not publish a separate postal address or email address on this site.
  </p>
</LegalDocument>
